  "problem": "What is $\\sqrt{{(-121)}^{2}}?$",
  "worked_solution": "Remember that by definition, the square root is always zero or positive, never negative.\n\nSo, the square root comes out to\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{(-121)^{2}}=\\sqrt{{121}^{2}}=121.\n$$",
